@api = http://localhost:5100
@keycloak = http://localhost:8180/realms/rbac-demo

### 1. Get a token for a test user (uses the test-only rbac-test-cli client; password = username)
#    Run this first; it stores the token for the requests below (Rider / JetBrains HTTP client syntax).
POST {{keycloak}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=rbac-test-cli&username=alice&password=alice

> {%
    client.global.set("token", response.body.access_token);
%}

### 2. Who am I? (any authenticated user)
GET {{api}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. List orders (order:read)
GET {{api}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Create order (order:write) - bob gets 403
POST {{api}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customer": "Acme Corp", "amount": 199.90 }

### 5. Delete order (order:delete) - only alice
DELETE {{api}}/api/orders/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Audit log (admin role) - only alice
GET {{api}}/api/admin/audit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
